{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When the day declines [לפנות ערב].</b> Like the sense of \"for the day declined [כי פנה היום]\" — this is also a strengthening according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory. And those who dispute say that לפנות is like לפני, but they have said nothing. And some say that its meaning is: when the evening begins to decline. And behold, after Scripture said לפנות ערב, it said \"and when the sun comes [וכבוא השמש]\" — behold, [this is] before evening. And similarly לפנות בקר is before the sun shines."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:28.204330176Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}